e":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:49:16.647Z","evidenceHash":"1adf3246a135057c7bff1693b98b52b8d9a9dd4a1e544a9f4d29745acb40d4b5"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-07T05:49:16.647Z","evidenceHash":"1adf3246a135057c7bff1693b98b52b8d9a9dd4a1e544a9f4d29745acb40d4b5"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/HXL.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/HXL.png","website":"https://www.hexcel.com","ceo":"Thomas C. Gentile","full_time_employees":"5563","description":"Hexcel Corporation, operating through its various subsidiaries, focuses on the innovation, production, and sale of advanced structural materials. These specialized materials are essential across the commercial aviation, space and defense, and broader industrial sectors. The company's operations are segmented into two primary divisions: Composite Materials and Engineered Products. The Composite Materials division is responsible for manufacturing and marketing a diverse range of products, including carbon fibers, specialized fabrics and reinforcements, prepregs, various fiber-reinforced matrix materials, robust structural adhesives, honeycomb structures, molding compounds, tooling solutions, polyurethane systems, and laminates. These materials are integral to the construction of military and commercial aircraft, wind turbine blades, recreational items, a wide array of industrial applications, and also find use in the automotive, marine, and railway industries. The Engineered Products segment concentrates on producing finished aircraft components and structural assemblies. This encompasses items such as wing-to-body fairings, wing panels, flight deck panels, door liners, rotorcraft blades, spars, and tip caps. Furthermore, it supplies structural sub-components and semi-finished parts that are incorporated into helicopter blades, engine nacelles, and various aircraft surfaces like flaps, wings, elevators, and fairings. Hexcel distributes its products both directly through its management, product specialists, and sales teams, and indirectly by utilizing independent distributors and authorized manufacturer representatives. Its market reach extends across the Americas, Europe, the Asia Pacific region, India, and Africa. Established in 1946, Hexcel Corporation maintains its corporate headquarters in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_en":"Hexcel Corporation, operating through its various subsidiaries, focuses on the innovation, production, and sale of advanced structural materials. These specialized materials are essential across the commercial aviation, space and defense, and broader industrial sectors. The company's operations are segmented into two primary divisions: Composite Materials and Engineered Products. The Composite Materials division is responsible for manufacturing and marketing a diverse range of products, including carbon fibers, specialized fabrics and reinforcements, prepregs, various fiber-reinforced matrix materials, robust structural adhesives, honeycomb structures, molding compounds, tooling solutions, polyurethane systems, and laminates. These materials are integral to the construction of military and commercial aircraft, wind turbine blades, recreational items, a wide array of industrial applications, and also find use in the automotive, marine, and railway industries. The Engineered Products segment concentrates on producing finished aircraft components and structural assemblies. This encompasses items such as wing-to-body fairings, wing panels, flight deck panels, door liners, rotorcraft blades, spars, and tip caps. Furthermore, it supplies structural sub-components and semi-finished parts that are incorporated into helicopter blades, engine nacelles, and various aircraft surfaces like flaps, wings, elevators, and fairings. Hexcel distributes its products both directly through its management, product specialists, and sales teams, and indirectly by utilizing independent distributors and authorized manufacturer representatives. Its market reach extends across the Americas, Europe, the Asia Pacific region, India, and Africa. Established in 1946, Hexcel Corporation maintains its corporate headquarters in Stamford, Connecticut.","description_zh":"Hexcel Corporation（美股代碼：HXL）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Aerospace & Defense 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"Two Stamford Plaza","city":"Stamford","state":"CT","zip":"06901-3261","country":"US","phone":"203 969 0666","full_address":"Two Stamford Plaza, Stamford, CT 06901-3261, US","range_52w":"67.38-111.74","year_high":111.74,"year_low":67.38,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":67.38,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-28","name":"KEATING NEAL J.","title":"director","is_buy":true,"action":"P-Purchase","shares":3000,"price":80.67,"total_val":0.24},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Hubbard Patricia","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":287,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Li David H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":340,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Li David H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":287,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-05","name":"Li David H","title":"director","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":340,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-09-08","name":"Lehman Gail E","title":"officer: See Remarks","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":8829,"price":68.15,"total_val":0.6},{"date":"2026-09-08","name":"Lehman Gail E","title":"officer: See Remarks","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":5000,